On the twenty-second day of my internship, I continued studying 
Linux process management. I learned how processes can run in
the foreground and background and studied commands such as jobs,
bg, and fg.

I also learned about the kill command and how signals can be 
sent to processes. I studied the basic purpose of commands
such as kill and pkill and learned why process management 
is important when working with Linux systems.

I followed the examples in the Linux book and reviewed 
additional explanations from The Missing Semester. 
These topics helped me understand how users can monitor 
and control processes directly from the terminal.
